# Security — IDOR, webhooks, secrets

Inspired by ECC common-security (MIT) + Lazy Developer Lock-It-Down; DIAL-tuned.

## Identity & AuthZ

- Authenticated ≠ authorized. After AuthN, **object-level** checks (`assertResourceAccess` or equiv) for jobs, orders, vehicles, promo_credits, delivery_jobs/offers, courier_locations.
- **Never** trust `userId` / `email` / `role` from body or query — JWT/session only.
- Authorize **before** cache read; user-scoped cache keys must include `userId`.

## Internal & webhooks

- Side-effect / worker / n8n / Temporal activity HTTP: fail closed if `INTERNAL_API_SECRET` (or mTLS) unset.
- All `/webhooks/*` (Paynow, ContiPay, EcoCash, PayPal, Meta WA, FDMS): verify signature **and** idempotency key/store before mutating.

## Secrets

- Never read/print/paste `.env*`. Refer by name only.
- Forbid `NEXT_PUBLIC_` / `VITE_` on `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, PSP keys, WA tokens, FDMS activation.
- Bundle-grep CI for `service_role`, `sk_live`, integration keys.

Audit-only prompts: `docs/agent-audits/`. Skills: `dial-rls-idor-audit`.
